Writer: a kit client sets the first-line indent in characters

Chinese text indents a paragraph's first line by two characters. The
core has held such an indent since 25.8 (SvxIndentValue in
FONT_CJK_ADVANCE, laid out by the font's own advance and written to
DOCX as w:firstLineChars), but FirstLineParaMargin's arguments carry
only an absolute length, so a kit client could not ask for it.
.uno:ElyFirstLineChars takes Chars, hundredths of a character, and
sets the selected paragraphs' first-line indent to that many CJK
advances. Its state is "hundredths,unit" for the indent in force, with
unit ic, em or twip, so a client can show an indent it did not set.

